              "query": "The user reports that messages sometimes disappear in Twake chat.",
              "content": "{\n\"candidates\": [\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Messages not syncing in Twake chat after deletion\",\n    \"issueSummary\": \"Messages that were deleted in Twake chat are still visible to some users or fail to sync properly.\",\n    \"rawKnowledge\": \"Users have reported that messages they have deleted in Twake chat remain visible to them or to other users. This can occur due to caching delays, replication issues, or sync conflicts between the client and server. The issue has been observed in both web and mobile clients. The problem is not consistent across all users and may be related to specific deployment configurations or network conditions.\",\n    \"whyPotentiallyRelevant\": \"The issue involves messages disappearing or not syncing in Twake chat, which is similar to the user's report of messages sometimes disappearing. The root cause may involve sync or replication issues, which could be related to the same underlying system behavior.\",\n    \"sourceHint\": \"internal_knowledge_base/chat_sync_issues.md\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"Twake chat messages not loading after refresh\",\n    \"issueSummary\": \"Users experience chat messages not loading or appearing to be stuck after refreshing the chat interface in Twake.\",\n    \"rawKnowledge\": \"A known issue has been reported where chat messages fail to load after a page refresh or navigation in Twake. This is typically caused by a race condition in the client-side rendering logic, where the initial fetch of messages is not properly handled. The issue has been observed in Chrome and Safari, and is more common in low-bandwidth or high-latency network conditions.\",\n    \"whyPotentiallyRelevant\": \"The issue involves chat messages not being visible after navigation or refresh, which is similar to the user's report of messages sometimes disappearing. The cause may be related to client-side rendering or network behavior.\",\n    \"sourceHint\": \"internal_knowledge_base/chat_rendering_bugs.md\"\n  }\n]\n}",
